WEBVTT

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.820
The House of Lancaster still clings
to the throne in defiance of reason.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.990
The same throne that they wrongfully
usurped from the House of York.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.570
Indeed. My father was executed
for the crime of treason,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.910
and our house plunged into dishonor.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:46.460
Your Grace's blood has always
been more noble than the king's.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.090
You have the stronger claim
to the throne, after all.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.010
Warwick, should I become king?

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.930
I swear on this white rose

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:03.270
that I will put you on the throne,
Your Majesty, King Richard.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:05.730
Father.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.860
I am going to rouse
a tempest in this land.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:14.280
I promise to return with
a golden circlet in hand.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.490
A golden circlet?

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.530
Within that circlet lies paradise.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.080
"Inspired by William Shakespeare"

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:24.080
Every joy and blessing
that the poets imagine.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.330
I want to fight alongside you, Father.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:31.800
I know. I hope you'll support me
on the battlefield when you're older.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.550
Richard, my son, I gave you my name,
and I have high hopes for you.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.970
Yes, Father!

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:41.760
My father is my light.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.850
Only he will save me
from darkness and gloom.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.530
"Original manga"
"Aya Kanno"

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.450
York of the white rose.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.120
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:10.540
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:15.210
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.110
Well, Richard, do you surrender?

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.070
That's Edward for you.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.410
Let me try again, Edward!

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.200
That's enough, Lord Richard.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.500
Your mother will scold you
if you're injured.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.840
Richard, go home with Catesby.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.630
Edward, let's race back to the house.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.550
Challenge accepted, George.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.550
See you later, Richard.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:02.640
Edward!

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.600
Catesby, give me your horse!

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.440
Lord Richard, it's too dangerous alone.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.520
Ride with me.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.860
I can do it!

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.660
I want to help my father soon.

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:30.160
I'll fight alongside him to win the throne
back from the Lancastrians.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.790
It will be my father's!

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.050
Mother!

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.460
Mother!

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.180
Witches live deep in the forest.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:45.600
That's why you must never go there alone.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.890
Mother?

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.320
Richard.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.570
--Mother.
--Richard!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.070
--Richard!
--Richard!

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.490
Richard!

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:04.950
Demon child! Did your mother abandon you?

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:05.950
Of course she did!

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:09.410
The day you were born,
a terrible storm laid trees low!

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.580
Owls screeched!

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:11.960
The night crows croaked!

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.330
To herald the coming
of an age of misfortune!

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.790
Your mother suffered
abnormal birthing pains!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.090
And after all that, her child...

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.550
...was a blood-soaked demon
who defied the will of God!

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.350
Let me prophecy, Richard.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:36.310
One day, a host of the elderly who have
lost their children, of widows, of orphans

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.610
will lament the untimely
deaths you have caused.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:46.360
"Why was he ever born?" they will cry,
as they curse the day of your birth!

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.490
Help!

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:54.830
That was dangerous!

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:57.670
Please! I think he's hurt.

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.300
A white boar.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.090
He might bite.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.350
Thank you for saving him.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:17.770
I just thought he'd make a good
addition to tonight's dinner.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:18.650
Mother!

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.400
What have you been doing? You're so dirty.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.490
George fell in the mud.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:25.320
Edward pushed me!

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.620
Come along, my sweet little
princes. Change your clothes.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:36.210
Are you hurt, Lord Richard?

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.540
Of course I'm not hurt.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.210
My father taught me horsemanship.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:47.630
When will I be able to
surpass my brothers?

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:57.100
When will my arms thicken?

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.770
When will I be able to be like my father?

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:06.650
I am a son of Richard Plantagenet,
Duke of York.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.450
I must be able to do it.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.830
His Grace has returned
from the battlefield.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:20.380
Finally! Father returns in triumph.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.880
Welcome home, Father!

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:24.090
Father!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.640
Richard, I almost didn't recognize you.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.900
I've improved my swordplay and learned to
ride full-grown horses like my brothers.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:45.110
Is that so? My, how you've grown.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:49.610
I swear to become a bold warrior
worthy of being a king's son.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.990
Father?

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:59.120
I was victorious in my battle
against the Lancastrians,

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:04.670
but the king begged me to guard
the people for his lifetime.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.760
Parliament strongly favored his petition,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.930
and I was forced to settle
for the title of Protector.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.890
I will not be king.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.390
Not while King Henry lives.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.190
Have they no shame?

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.020
Let's fight them again!

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.320
The crown belongs on your head, Father!

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:30.280
Richard.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.450
We'll force them to acknowledge you!

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:34.950
But...

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:35.870
Father.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.040
"Within that circlet lies paradise.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.500
Every joy and blessing
that the poets imagine."

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.050
You told me that yourself, Father.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.880
Let us fight.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.430
We'll dye this white rose red
with Henry's blood!

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:54.640
Father!

00:07:58.810 --> 00:07:59.930
Gentlemen,

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:03.100
I will cross swords with
the Lancastrians once more.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:09.150
This storm will rage until a golden
crown gleams upon my brow!

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.450
Sharpen your swords and prepare for war!

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:19.410
I will become king.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.250
I know.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.370
I'll help you, Father.

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:26.710
No. You're still too young
to give your life.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:29.550
But Father,
I've been training to fight for--

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.970
Preserve my name, Richard.
It's the name of a king.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.810
Richard! Give up already.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:43.640
We're still kids.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.070
Damn it!

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.250
You can't do it, Richard.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.960
Not with your body.

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:13.590
Who are you?!

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.300
I'm Joan of Arc.

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:19.850
I'm you.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:24.430
Speak sense, you French witch!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.060
How could you be me?!

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:30.940
I know everything there is
to know about you, Richard.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:34.110
Even the secret you keep hidden.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:36.030
Here. Take a look.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.780
Your body...

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.490
...is neither a man's nor a woman's.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.210
Lord Richard!

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.870
--I beg your--
--It's too late for that.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.710
You and my parents are the only
people who know about this.

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.720
A demon child.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.640
Lord Richard.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.140
I've had enough!

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.390
You mustn't!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.020
Your body is precious.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:20.700
You ugly boar.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.950
You're just like me.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:45.220
Your Grace, the men are
fatigued from this long battle.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.020
I suggest a withdrawal.

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.020
A king stands firm.

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:49.270
--But as things stand--
--I promised Richard that I would fight
until the bitter end!

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:53.060
--I promised Richard that I would fight
until the bitter end!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.530
Has Father returned?

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.990
Are you York's son?

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:10.830
To a Lancastrian victory!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.630
To our King Henry!

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:19.590
O Lord, please guard my husband and son.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:23.050
Mother, I'm sure that Father
and Edward are fine.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:24.720
Right, Richard?

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:25.560
Father...

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:31.520
You demon! This only happened because you
beguiled him with your honeyed words!

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:34.360
--Mother?
--When you spoke to him...

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:38.900
...your face was the very picture
of a devil!

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.400
You are a demon child!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.740
--What's wrong, Mother?
--You just don't know, George.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:47.870
A demon dwells within his body!

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.590
Demon child!

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:02.050
O Lord,

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:06.300
preserve my husband and son
from the devil's clutches.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.020
Father!

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.860
Father, are you safe?

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:28.870
Where am I?

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:47.800
Who's there? What are you doing?

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.940
I'm making a sundial.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.320
Here, I'll show you.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:10.370
You watch each minute pass

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:16.080
and ponder how many minutes
and years make up a person's life.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:18.340
You're an odd man.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:20.750
All shepherds do this.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.130
Are you a shepherd?

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.010
Me?

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:26.930
Yes!

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.600
You count the time and then divide it up.

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.770
How many hours spent herding flocks?

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:37.690
Days until the ewes get with child?
Weeks until they give birth?

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:40.860
Years until you shear the lambs?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.940
What a delightful life it must be.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:48.070
Shepherds are lucky. You have it easy.

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:49.910
I suppose so.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:52.950
This world is nothing
but tragedy and desire.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:57.790
Shepherds are far happier than kings.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:59.420
That can't be!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:02.090
Paradise lies within that royal crown!

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:09.930
Meeting you here delights
me more than any crown.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.140
Come. Join me.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:22.570
Hey!

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:29.030
I have nightmares under
a canopy, but never here.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.450
Do you ever have nightmares?

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:37.750
What kind of nightmares?

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.630
I often dream of my mother abandoning me.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:50.140
But in the end, God always reaches
down a hand of light to me.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:56.770
Light...

00:14:56.770 --> 00:15:02.190
"Why was he ever born?" they will cry,
as they curse the day of your birth!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.070
Father.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.580
My light isn't God.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:23.040
I'm sure that Death would come
for you if you went to sleep here.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:28.510
That might not be so bad,
if my death could save someone.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:33.300
What difference would the
death of one shepherd make?

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:34.760
That's true.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:39.310
I like you!

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:42.520
You're right. I'm just a shepherd.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:46.900
In the end, God will call me to
His side just like everyone else.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:52.660
I don't want to die.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:55.950
I'm sure I couldn't go to heaven if I did.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.330
I mean, I'm...

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.040
...a demon child.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:10.010
That's why I can't get
my mother to love me.

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:20.390
I'll pray for you.
Would you tell me your name?

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:23.600
Richard.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.730
My name is Henry.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:33.530
Richard, would you be my friend?

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.370
Then, let's stay here forever.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.210
I'm sure you won't freeze.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.670
Not if you hold each other close.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:48.800
Are you going back to that cell again?

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:51.380
Poor little Richard.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:54.970
You know that no one will love you.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:17:00.180
My father will shine
his light into any prison.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:04.270
My duty is to guard
my mother until he does!

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:12.240
"Henry."

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.530
I hate to even speak that name.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.200
Hey! Wake up!

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.160
I've been waiting for you, Richard.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.410
You look great in those shackles.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:25.710
Just like a bear before
the hounds torment it to death.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.540
I guess that makes you a dog, then.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.500
You can act brave and bite,

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.970
but one swipe of a forepaw will send you
off with your tail between your legs.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:37.680
Don't get cocky, you filthy demon.

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:39.890
Your body holds a secret.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.390
Isn't that what your mother told you?

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.520
The jailer told me.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.850
Have you got a devil's tail?

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:51.230
Or are you hiding a beast's
body under your clothes?

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:53.110
Let's find out.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:10.840
Stop spouting pointless insults
and learn from your father's piety.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.510
You'll be dining in heaven tonight.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.880
Hey. Stop it.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.300
You ugly demon.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.800
Your brutality is proof of what you are!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.350
Stop it!

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:35.070
He's... a woman?

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:37.820
Hurry! The Yorkists are coming!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.950
You there! What are you doing?!

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.370
Richard!

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.040
Edward!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.540
Edward, Mother is...

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.460
Don't worry. We just saved them both.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:53.800
Our forces have already occupied
London and captured Henry.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:55.710
We've won!

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.470
Henry of Lancaster...

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:03.430
...offer His Grace the throne.

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:07.930
Henry, the House of York
will inherit the throne.

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:11.600
There is no need to stain the ground
of England with any more blood.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.780
Long live His Grace, the Duke of York!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.700
Edward, you've served your father well.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.280
I'm proud of you.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.410
You were truly magnificent.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:29.290
No heir could be more worthy.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.290
I'm not the best.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:34.250
With this, your reign
has practically begun.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.840
No, I'm not king yet.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.590
As long as Henry lives--

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.090
In that case, Father,

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.640
you should execute Henry at once.

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:48.850
Wait, Richard. Henry still has his uses.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:53.480
We should proceed with caution until
parliament recognizes His Grace's claim.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.650
I suggest we enjoy this banquet first.

00:19:56.650 --> 00:20:01.450
My daughters are anxious
to dance with the princes.

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:02.780
The girl from the woods.

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.830
I-I never said anything
about wanting to dance.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.500
I'll excuse myself.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:12.920
Where are you going?!

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.500
I'm a poor dancer.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:21.170
Well... I actually can't dance either.

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:24.180
I'd rather spend my time learning
swordsmanship than dancing.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.970
I like swordplay better too!

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.220
You do?!

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:31.060
You're an odd girl.

00:20:31.060 --> 00:20:34.650
Y-You're quite strange yourself.

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:39.860
You're... different from
everyone else, somehow.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.700
Don't get the wrong idea, Richard.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.660
You're not like anyone else.

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.710
You're "different"!

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.210
You're all alone!

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:06.850
Once you go to war, even Edward
may not be a match for you, Richard.

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.300
Father.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:14.980
I heard your voice on the battlefield--
telling me that a king keeps fighting.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:19.820
I felt a special bond between us then,

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.150
Richard.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:27.120
As your father, I swear to never
retreat from battle again.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.620
I swear too!

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.960
I swear that I'll take
Henry's head myself!

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:40.460
I'm not a king anymore.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:43.420
I'm just a shepherd.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:45.550
I long to see you,

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:46.890
Richard.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:58.270
Father, if it would help to make you king,

00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:00.980
I would even slay God.
